; The guard (DESIGN.md, "Shared state and the query hook"): the build gives
; an error if a library of Cistern depends on unix, on threads or on a world
; of weft. weft.linux and weft.kqueue depend on weft.posix, thus the forbidden
; weft.posix also forbids these two worlds. -linkall links each module of the
; libraries, thus a module that no other module uses also gets the check. The
; windtrap suites link unix, thus the guard is a separate executable with no
; test library.

(test
 (name nounix)
 (libraries
  cistern
  cistern.core
  cistern.names
  cistern.schema
  cistern.sql
  cistern.mysql)
 (link_flags (-linkall))
 (forbidden_libraries unix threads.posix weft.posix weft.sim weft.os))
